  "title": "# Build train map: a subway/train-schedule diagram of every build Brett (Nov 1 2026): \"a map type t…",
  "asked": "# Build train map: a subway/train-schedule diagram of every build Brett (Nov 1 2026): \"a map type thing, like a physical thing where you see this, that, done, like a diagram, like a train schedule where you see where the train's at.\" Read CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, _claude/THREADS.md first. ## What it looks like - Each build = a train LINE (own colour from the theme tokens, label = build name + owning agent). - Each step = a STOP on the line. Done stops filled, current stop pulsing, pending stops hollow, failed/blocked stops red with an icon. - A TRAIN marker (the agent's avatar/ID-card badge) sits on the stop that agent is on right now, animated along the line as steps complete (live updates). - Lines that depend on each other connect at transfer stations (shared dependencies / merged-into builds). - Tap a stop: popup with step name, model, agent, start/finish time, duration, commit/PR link, open in Steps view. Tap a line: open the build. Tap a train: open the agent (agent-history). - Filters: profile, agent, status (running / today / all), hide finished lines. Pinch-zoom + pan on phones, fits the screen on desktop. Legend. - Lives as a view on the Builds page toolbar (\"Map\"), in the Breakroom, and as an attachable widget for banners/home. ## Data: NO new datasets Read only the one builds store, orchestrator profiles, agent-swarm leases, agent-jobs run records. Reuse whatever agent<->step link `agent-history` adds (running build on branch claude/agent-history); if it isn't on main yet, merge origin/main often and build against the same fields, backward compatible. The Builds page is being finished by `builds-one-page-finish`; add the Map view through its view registry/extension point, don't fork the page. ## Reuse + rules The map is a framework control (SVG renderer) driven by a hot-swappable asset (map style: line thickness, stop shapes, colours, animation) reading scale tokens; new asset type registered on both validators with schema + fixture if needed. Plugin deps declared in plugin.json requirements; plugin-lifecycle green. Phone-first. Orchestrator build `build-train-map` in profile `refactor`, steps <= 30 min. Tests, lifecycle + theme checks, phone + desktop screenshots, report `_claude/builds/reports/build-train-map.md`, THREADS row, STATUS. ## Landing Commit on this branch, merge origin/main, push the branch. Do NOT push to main; Brett's session lands it with build_land. Never print secrets. End with a short report. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
